From: shadaytree <82917003+shadaytree@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:04:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): a "parameters are not usable" refusal names the
 field and its rule

Adding or editing an operation with a bad number, such as a 2D Pocket
stepdown of -3, was refused with "operation parameters are not usable
for a 2D Pocket operation", which does not say which field is wrong.

When is_sane fails, the commands now read the parameters in their
project and MCP field names and add the first shared field that breaks
its rule: stepdown, stepover, feed, plunge_feed, tolerance and
helix_radius must be greater than 0, and stock_to_leave must be 0 or
more. For example: "... for a 2D Pocket operation: stepdown must be
greater than 0 (got -3)". Other causes keep the old sentence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Fixes #3545
